attorneys.bio:
Donovan DeLuca represents individuals in every phase of divorce, dissolution of marriage, legal separation, adoption, child custody, and child support matters for unmarried parents. Donovan is also an experienced litigator from his time in the Geauga County Prosecutor’s Office representing Children Services. While Donovan focuses his practice in Family Law, he is very knowledgeable about Juvenile Law, Criminal Defense and Civil Litigation. Donovan draws from his personal experiences to empathize with his clients as he assists them in navigating their matter.

His practice includes the following areas:

• Dividing complex marital estates, including investment properties, business interests, unusual investments, complicated retirement plans, and separate property issues;

• Evaluating business and partnership interests for division in divorce;

• Researching and analyzing records to identify misappropriated or hidden marital assets;

• Drafting, interpreting, and evaluating the enforceability of prenuptial and postnuptial agreements;

• Crafting tailored temporary and permanent spousal and child support plans;

• Allocating parental rights and responsibilities;

• Issues concerning parental relocation;

• Custody matters involving psychological expert testimony;

• Domestic violence matters; and

• Handling post-decree issues of enforcement and non-disclosed or omitted assets.

• Handling children services cases.

In his spare time, Donovan loves to watch men and women’s sports, football, basketball, baseball, track and the Olympics. You may find him at the local YMCA exercising, or at a board meeting. Donovan volunteers for the Cleveland Metropolitan Bar Association’s Cleveland Legal Collaborative but prioritizes his family by spending time with his wife and daughter Kennedy.

